# Development Rules

## Agent Behavior

If a requested change conflicts with the design system or architecture defined in these rules, explain the conflict before making the change — don't silently override it.

Review every change as a Senior Angular Engineer would before a production deployment: correctness, performance, accessibility, and maintainability, not just "does it run."

## Angular

Always use

- Standalone Components
- Signals
- computed()
- inject()
- Reactive Forms
- Control Flow (@if @for)

Use effect() only when necessary.

Never use

- NgModules
- any
- constructor injection when inject() is sufficient

Always enable strict typing.

Use interfaces.

Prefer readonly properties.

Keep templates clean.

Keep business logic outside templates.

---

## Zoneless + Third-Party Libraries

This app runs Zoneless Change Detection. Embla Carousel and Lucide Angular (and any other non-Angular-native library) do not know about Angular's change detection and will not trigger view updates on their own.

When integrating them:

- Wrap any state derived from a third-party callback/event in a signal, and update that signal explicitly inside the callback.
- Never rely on a library's internal DOM mutation to reflect state in the template — read the library's state into a signal and drive the template off the signal.
- Test carousel interactions (slide change, drag) manually to confirm the UI actually updates, since this is the most likely place zoneless bugs will surface silently.

