## Component Rules

One responsibility per component.

Search existing components before creating new ones — check `shared/ui` first.

Never duplicate components.

Never duplicate styles.

Reuse everything possible.

Keep components small.

Prefer composition over inheritance.

Follow the project structure defined in design-system.md.

---

## Performance

The assessment brief explicitly asks for a 100/100 Lighthouse Performance score. Treat 100 as the real target, not an afterthought — SSR, hydration, zoneless, optimized images, minimal JS, local fonts, and code splitting should all be working together to get there.

Target

100 Performance (95+ is the acceptable floor only if a genuine trade-off prevents 100)

95+ Accessibility

95+ SEO

95+ Best Practices

Never strip real functionality, animation, or font loading purely to chase the last few Lighthouse points. If hitting a perfect 100 would require sacrificing real UX quality, keep the UX and document the trade-off and the achieved score in the README.

Use

- SSR
- Hydration
- Zoneless
- NgOptimizedImage
- Lazy Loading
- Tree Shaking
- Code Splitting
- Local Fonts
- SVG Icons
- TransferState

Avoid

- Bootstrap
- jQuery
- GSAP
- AOS
- Heavy animation libraries
- Video backgrounds
- Particle systems

---

## Animations

Use CSS first.

Use Motion One only if CSS is not enough.

Animate only

- transform
- opacity

Recommended animations

- Fade In
- Slide Up
- Scale
- Lift
- Count Up
- Glass Navbar Transition

Never animate

- width
- height
- top
- left

Animation duration

200ms

300ms

500ms

Use ease-out.

Animations should feel premium but never distract the user.

---

## Accessibility

Use Semantic HTML.

Support keyboard navigation.

Provide ARIA labels.

Always include alt text.

Maintain proper color contrast.

Use visible focus states.

---

## SEO

Only one H1.

Use semantic heading hierarchy.

Generate meaningful meta title and description.

Include Open Graph metadata.

Use structured data where appropriate.

---

## Content

Use clearly-fictional placeholder copy unless real Digital Bond content is provided. Never invent real client names, real statistics, or real press mentions. Mark placeholder content with a code comment (e.g. `// TODO: replace placeholder stat`) so it's easy to find before launch.

---

## Contact Form

Route submission through `ContactService.submit()` returning an Observable. Do not hardcode a specific backend call directly in the component — see project.md for the pending decision on submission target.

On success, open the shared Modal component to show the success pop-up and update the URL to `/done` via Angular Router (`Router.navigate`), never `window.location` — see project.mdc for the full required flow.

---

## Before Writing Any Code

Think first.

Reuse before creating.

Never generate duplicate code.

Follow the Design System.

Optimize every decision for readability, scalability, maintainability, accessibility, and performance.

Generate production-ready Angular code only.
